    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Optimization</title>
            <p component="b" workspace="1in">
                Thinking outside of the mathematics context, what does it mean to optimize something?
            </p>
            <p component="a">
                Thinking outside of the mathematics context, what does it mean to optimize something? To make it as good as possible, for whatever good means.
            </p>

            <p component="b" workspace="3in">
                How do we formulate this idea mathematically?
            </p>
            <p component="a">
                How do we formulate this idea mathematically? Maximizing or minimizing an objective function on an interval with respect to some constraints. All of these parts come out of the word problem that is given to you. Once you do that, it's a standard calc problem.
            </p>

        </paragraphs>
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find the maximum value of the function <m>f(x) = x(10-x)</m> on the interval <m>[0,10]</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find the maximum possible product of two non-negative numbers whose sum is <m>10</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Optimization Process</title>
            <p component="b" workspace="5in">
                How can we summarize the process of applied optimization?
            </p>
            <p component="a">
                How can we summarize the process of applied optimization? Picture, objective, constraints, combine, interval. Solve, restate.
            </p>

        </paragraphs>
    </page>

<page>
